# SwiftFormat: the house style, checked on every commit and in CI.
# `Scripts/quality/tool swiftformat .` fixes a file; docs/quality.md has the rest.
#
# The options below write down the style the code already has (four spaces,
# `0..<n` without spaces, `case .x(let y)`, one-line guards, aligned
# continuation lines), so the formatter keeps it instead of rewriting it.

--swift-version 6.2
--language-mode 6
--min-version 0.63.1

--exclude .build,**/.build,DerivedData,build

--indent 4
--ifdef no-indent
--ranges no-space
--decimal-grouping ignore
--hex-grouping ignore
--pattern-let inline
--trailing-commas collections-only
--strip-unused-args closure-only
--type-blank-lines preserve
--else-position same-line
--guard-else auto
--wrap-arguments preserve
--wrap-parameters preserve
--wrap-collections preserve

# Rules that would rewrite a deliberate part of the style:
# - indent, wrapArguments: the code aligns wrapped lines under the opening paren
#   or operator, which these rules flatten.
# - wrap*Bodies, wrapMultilineStatementBraces: one-line `guard … else { return }`
#   and `{` at the end of a wrapped condition are the norm here.
# - sortImports: imports go system first, then the project's own modules.
# - modifierOrder: `nonisolated` comes first (`nonisolated private static`).
# - swiftTestingTestCaseNames: tests keep camelCase names, not `raw identifiers`.
# - blankLinesAtStartOfScope, redundantSelf, hoistTry, hoistAwait,
#   trailingClosures, redundantType, redundantMemberwiseInit: spacing and
#   spelling choices left to the author.
# - preferKeyPath: `#expect(xs.allSatisfy(\.flag))` does not compile, because
#   the macro passes the key path on to a rethrowing call.
--disable preferKeyPath
--disable indent,wrapArguments
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapIfExpressionBodies,wrapPropertyBodies,wrapFunctionBodies,wrapLoopBodies,wrapMultilineStatementBraces
--disable sortImports,modifierOrder,swiftTestingTestCaseNames
--disable blankLinesAtStartOfScope,redundantSelf,hoistTry,hoistAwait,trailingClosures,redundantType,redundantMemberwiseInit
